 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to validate certain acts of the North Syracuse central school district\nwith regard to certain capital improvement projects",
    "basePrintNo": "S8763",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8763-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 53,
       "fullName": "David J. Valesky",
       "imgName": "395_david_j._valesky.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 395,
       "sessionMemberId": 951,
       "sessionYear": 2017,
       "shortName": "VALESKY"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8763\n\nSPONSOR: DEFRANCISCO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to validate certain acts of the North Syracuse central school\ndistrict with regard to certain capital improvement projects\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nRelates to the school construction contracts for the North Syracuse\nCentral School District.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill legalizes any final cost report submitted by the North Syra-\ncuse Central School District for approved school construction projects\nand payments of building aid for such projects shall not be reduced due\nto any failure of the district to submit such final cost reports in a\ntimely manner. The legalized projects are: numbers 5037-010, 0003-007,\n0011-012, 7999-001, 0016-019 and 0009-014.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe North Syracuse Central School District made an error and did not\nfile the appropriate paperwork in an acceptable period of time. Due to\nthis error, the state is requiring the district to pay back funds that\nthe school district has previously received. Failure to forgive this\nfiling error would create undue fiscal hardship for the school district.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nThis bill would save the school district approximately $2,000,000 a year\nfor the next ten years.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "printNo": "S8763",
