  "chapter": 200,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                 APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 1 Chapter 200\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 8763, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  validate  certain  acts  of the North Syracuse central\n        school district  with  regard  to  certain  capital  improvement\n        projects\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  The  law  governing  state  building  aid  payment  on  school capital\nprojects was changed in 2011 in order to address pre-payment issues  and\nresulting  penalties  to  school districts. However, a handful of school\ndistricts have subsequently discovered outstanding final cost reports on\nschool projects that predated the 2011 change  in  the  law,  subjecting\nthem  to the large building aid penalty. In some cases, such as the case\nof the North Syracuse School District, this has resulted in  a  substan-\ntial  financial  penalty due to an administrative error. This bill would\naddress North  Syracuse's  unusually  high  penalty  by  validating  the\ndistrict's  final  cost  reports  for  the capital projects in question,\nthereby forgiving the assessed penalty.\n \n  In 2017 and 2018, the Legislature and I adopted payment provisions  in\nthe  Budget  to  further mitigate outstanding filing penalties for these\nschool  districts.  These  changes  mainly  benefitted  smaller   school\ndistricts  with  larger  penalties  relative  to  their overall budgets,\nhowever North Syracuse's penalty was so high,  that  it  was  not  fully\nhelped  by  the budget changes. North Syracuse's outstanding penalty was\nreduced from $29.9 million to $19.2 million by these budget  provisions,\nbut the remaining penalty is still considerably high, in fact, it is the\nhighest in the state by far.\n \n  This $19.2 million penalty, by its sheer size, is distinguishable from\npenalties  against  all  other  school  districts, which are much lower.\nAlthough previous similar bills have traditionally been  vetoed  outside\nof  the  budget process, assessment of this unusually high penalty would\nresult in considerably less resources for the  students  of  the  school\ndistrict and would have a devastating effect on educational programming.\nThe  school  district has also indicated that it could face depletion of\nall of its cash reserves if this bill is not enacted.\n \n  Therefore, due to the excessively high amount of this penalty, and its\nresulting disparate negative impact on the students of the  North  Syra-\ncuse School District, I am signing this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2018
 },
